{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/167693-werewolf-antagonist-the-broodmother","id":167693,"title":"Werewolf Antagonist: The Broodmother","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-13T02:40:17-07:00","id":167693,"title":"Werewolf Antagonist: The Broodmother","content":"I was thinking of starting a Werewolf game to test PenDragon's GMC werewolf fix. I wanted to structure the campaign around a central threat, something dangerous, and something that would give some more experienced Uratha a run for their money, and be strange enough to surprise the players. So I decided to look through the various antagonist books I have, and came upon the Mother from <i>Predators. </i>It sparked an idea, one of werewolves versus the Zerg <i>ala Starcraft</i> and the idea brought a devious smile to my face. So I am restructuring the Mother in the image of the Tyranid, and the Zerg. So here's my notes on it.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i><b>The Broodmother<br /> <img src=\"https://lh6.googleusercontent.com/-7N_OGAQlhuw/AAAAAAAAAAI/AAAAAAAAAY8/sLcVJ161M9U/photo.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></b></i></span><br /> According to one all-but-forgotten tale, when Luna descended to the earth, her handmaidens walked with her. They were the ones to draw away the rejected suitors so that Luna could be alone with Father Wolf, and when her time there was done, they ascended back to the sky with her. All but one. One of her handmaidens decided to tarry, taking her leisure with Luna\u2019s rejected suitors and enjoying the delights of the flesh. She was still there when the Gauntlet rose, and became flesh forevermore.<br /> <br /> At least, that is what the people whisper, when the name, [First Tongue Name], comes up. The truth may be far stranger.<br /> <br /> From places unknown did the Broodmother come from, and it came to assimilate everything to be part of its' Brood.<br /> <br /> The Broodmother is a grotesque creature that stands taller than an Uratha in Gauru form. It's body is covered in a layer of thick hide, made partly of chitin and knotted muscles. Behind it is a mockery of a womb, a long, nearly transparent, sack that glows in a sickly light, dark shadows seem to flit below the skin; larvae and it's children. It's large body is supported by six, strong, bladed limbs.<br /> <br /> (Ugh, not so good at fluff writing right now -.-)<br /> <br /> Alright, so in my game, the truth behind the Broodmother is that it's part of biological weapon designed by the Ancients (the one's who created humanity) and when the <i>Hisil</i> and material were closer. In simplest terms, the Broodmother takes Essence and genetic materials and births monsters, until they wipe out the everything on the planet. However, it was corrupted and the Brood seeks to make the perfect creature, the pinnacle of evolution. That's why it wants Uratha, to assimilate their shapechanging into the Swarm.<br /> <br /> Anyways, my idea for the campaign is for a corporation of humans to dig it up with the intent to exploit it. They'll be the first antagonists, what it'll start with. However, they unleash the Broodmother which begins to multiply. They attack, capture and assimilate Uratha. It'll involve protecting their territory, convincing other packs to help, and even humans learning about it. There'll be repercussions in the Hisil, my idea is the psychic influence of the Brood causes spirits to become more likely to go <i>Magath</i>, devour other spirits in a grotesque mockery of the Brood's own drive to eat, and assimilate everything to become the perfect creature.<br /> <br /> And now the Stats of the Broodmother.<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes</b>: Intelligence 4, Wits 5, Resolve 5, Strength 7,<br /> Dexterity 4, Stamina 9, Presence 6, Manipulation 3, Composure<br /> 5<br /> <b>Skills</b>: Medicine 3, Occult 3, Athletics 2, Brawl 5, Stealth 1,<br /> Survival 3, Animal Ken 1, Empathy 6, Expression 1, Intimidation<br /> 3, Subterfuge 1<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Ambidextrous, Danger Sense, Direction Sense,<br /> Iron Stamina 3, Iron Stomach, Natural Immunity, Toxin<br /> Resistance<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Potency</b>: 6<br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Patience<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Lust<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 8<br /> <b>Defense</b>: 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 17 (species factor 7)<br /> <b>Size:</b> 11<br /> <b>WEAPONS/ATTACKS</b>:<br /> <b>Type Damage Dice Pool</b><br /> Scythe 3 (L) 13<br /> Bite* 4 (L) 12<br /> Claw 2 (L) 12<br /> <br /> *Can only be used in a Grapple.<br /> <b>ARMOR:</b><br /> <b>Type Rating Defense Penalty</b><br /> Thick hide 2/3 0<br /> <br /> <b>Health:</b> 20<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 25<br /> <b>Numina</b>: Awe, Telekinesis, Emotional Aura, Implant Mission<br /> <b>\u2022 Spawn:</b> The Brood mother can spawn three larvae as a<br /> standard action for a point of Willpower,alternatively, the<br /> Broodmother can spawn one Broodling, The newborn<br /> broodling takes one turn to get its bearings,and then<br /> can begin attacking its Mother\u2019s assailants or otherwise<br /> carrying out its progenitor\u2019s will. Newborn spawn are of<br /> course the weakest of the brood, and should be given<br /> appropriate statistics.<br /> <b>\u2022 Empathic:</b> The Broodmother communicates by receiving<br /> and broadcasting emotions. It can effectively sense the<br /> emotions of anyone within 100 yards, and can \u201cread\u201d a<br /> specific person\u2019s emotions in more detail as easily as a person<br /> observes another person\u2019s clothing. It may attempt to<br /> broadcast its own emotions as a means of communication.<br /> Actively sifting through these emotions to understand the<br /> gist of what the Mother is attempting to \u201csay\u201d requires a<br /> Composure + Empathy roll. Success establishes some measure<br /> of context (\u201cIt wants us to leave\u201d), and exceptional<br /> success provides greater context (\u201cIt recognizes us as old<br /> enemies but doesn\u2019t want to fight us yet\u201d).<br /> <b>\u2022 Brood Control:</b> The Mother is in constant telepathic<br /> communication with all of its spawn that remain<br /> within 200 yards. Unlike communication with outsiders,<br /> the Mother and its spawn instinctively understand one<br /> another, and can communicate as effectively as if they<br /> were using language. The psychic presence of the Broodmother<br /> can control the Swarm, giving them purpose and intelligence.<br /> Any spawn under the Broodmother's psychic control has<br /> its Intelligence, Resolve and Composure traits increased by 2.<br /> <b>\u2022 Infection: </b>The Broodmother can infect a living target with<br /> Brood parasites. Spend 3 Essence to releases a cloud of<br /> eggs which latch onto the either through breath or burrowing<br /> into their skin. When infected, the parasites rewrite the genetic<br /> material of the target, and pump them full of the Mother's vile<br /> Essence, turning it into a Brood, and allowing it to be controlled<br /> by the Broodmother.<br /> (Any help with a system for this?)<br /> <b>\u2022 Regeneration:</b> The Mother regains either three<br /> wounds of lethal damage or four wounds of bashing<br /> damage each turn as a reflexive action. It will regenerate<br /> lethal damage first, regenerating bashing only when no<br /> more lethal damage is left on its health track. Aggravated<br /> damage is healed at the rate of two levels per day.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the Infected, I'd probably base it off the system for Claiming a victim.<br /> <br /> Anyways, any idea for story seeds of Brood, or any ways you could see this refined, and expanded on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":1601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","user":"Dreaminggod","date":". 06-13-2014, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T09:03:28-07:00","id":167960,"title":"","content":"Thanks for sharing Dreaminggod. I am currently running a nomad pack who specializes in helping fix territories and hunting down the worse that both worlds have to offer. This lovely lady is going to be a great addition!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1883-face_plont","name":"Face_Plont","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1883_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T09:51:24-07:00","id":168006,"title":"","content":"Well, that's the greatest compliment one can give. xD Tell me how it goes, and if you make any tweaks; I'd be interested to know ahead of time. If you're interested, I was going to write out some sample warriors, and infected later tonight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T10:22:04-07:00","id":168042,"title":"","content":"As a good GM, I am always willing to take ideas from everything I read and discuss with others <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> You said you were looking for ideas concerning a system for the infected. After some thought I remembered the Thralls of the Worm created by Zmai, the Worm, also in the last section of the Predators book. Pretty basic abilities: <b>Fortified- </b>+2 dots all physical traits, <b>Fearless- </b>+3 bonus to resist intimidation or fear effects, <b>No Will of Their Own- </b>-5 penalty to contradict the Worm.<br /> <br /> Pretty good to start, one thing that I was thinking was maybe adding gradual growth of chitin on the skin that would give natural armor after a certain period of infection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1883-face_plont","name":"Face_Plont","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1883_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T10:30:41-07:00","id":168078,"title":"","content":"Hmm. That's not a bad idea. My initial thought, as I said, was to base it off Claiming. Give them evolution points, but, perhaps that's a good start. <br /> <br /> &quot;Upon Infection, the Infected gain <b>Armored Growths</b>- 1/1 Armor, <b>Physical Enhancement</b>- +2 to all Physical attributes, <b>No Will of Their Own- </b>-5 penalty to contradict the Broodmother, and <b>Evolution</b>- x amount of Evolution points to spend on Aspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T07:52:54-07:00","id":168930,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Brood Infested Human</b></span><br /> <br /> When the infestation reaches critical stages it starts to twist the flesh and bone of the infected, strengthening muscles, bones and evolving weaponry to make one an effective killing machine. The will of the person is subsumed, and their memories stripped from them and transferred to the Hivemind of the Brood. All that is left is a feral killing machine, it's will inexorably tied to the will of the Broodmother. <br /> <b>Description</b>: The figure was once a man, or a woman, but now it's nothing but a shambling horror. It's eyes are twin pinpricks of crimson, like burning coals. It's skin its leathery with misshapen, hulking muscles. It's jaw is split in twain, you can see fangs where teeth once where, and a tube that looks as if it's a writhing centipede, runs down it's neck, and disappears into it's chest. It makes a strange, constant growling sound. The only thing it can say is, &quot;For the Swarm...&quot; in a hollow, buzzing voice. The infested's hands are morphed into a mockery of the human hand, it's fingers are lengthened to to extreme lengths the skin and nails replaced by a dull grey chitin sharper than a knife.<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Intelligence 1, Wits 3, Resolve 2, Strength 4,<br /> Dexterity 4, Stamina 4, Presence 1, Manipulation 1, Composure<br /> 3<br /> <b>Skills</b>: Athletics 2, Brawl 4, Stealth 2, <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Danger Sense, Iron Stamina 3, Iron Stomach, Natural Immunity,<br /> Toxin Resistance<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 5<br /> <b>Potency</b>: 1<br /> <b>Virtue:</b> -<br /> <b>Vice:</b> -<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 8<br /> <b>Defense</b>: 7<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13 (species factor 5)<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>WEAPONS/ATTACKS</b>:<br /> <b>Type Damage Dice Pool</b><br /> Claw 2 (L) 8<br /> <br /> <b>ARMOR:</b><br /> <b>Type Rating Defense Penalty</b><br /> Thick hide 2/1 0<br /> <br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 5<br /> <b>Aspects:</b> Immune to Pain <b>\u2022</b>, Inhuman Reflexes <b>\u2022\u2022</b>, Natural Weaponry <b>\u2022\u2022</b>,<br /> Dark Sight <b>\u2022\u2022</b> <br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 No Will of It's Own</b>: The Infested does not have a will of it's own. It is<br /> connected to the Hivemind and receives a -5 to any attempt to harm, or<br /> contradict the Brood's wishes.<br /> <b>\u2022 Regeneration: </b>The Infested regains one point of Bashing or Lethal<br /> damage per round. It will prioritize Lethal above Bashing.<br /> <b>\u2022 Physical Perfection:</b> The Swarm virus improves all organic matter <br /> it comes in contact with. Improve the Infected's physical attributes by<br /> two each.<br /> <b>\u2022 Armored Growths</b>: The mutagenic properties of the virus stimulate cell<br /> growth and hardening, all Infest receive 2/1 armor.<br /> <b>\u2022 Fearless:</b> The Infested is fearless, and cares not for it's own safety, it <br /> will gladly sacrifice itself for the Hive, and the Brood. The Infected has a<br /> +3 bonus to resist all supernatural attempts to induce Fear or<br /> Intimidation.<br /> <b>\u2022 </b> <b>For the Swarm!</b>:The Brood regains a point of Willpower every time it takes <br /> a beneficial action for the Swarm. It can only happen once per event (e.g. It will get <br /> a point of Willpower for intercepting and attacking a threat, but it won't get a new point<br /> \u200bevery round it attacks.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Brood Drone</span></b><br /> The Brood Drone is one of the most basic genetic templates within the larvae's code; it is the beginning of the Hive and one of the most protected of the Brood. Found almost exclusively within the Hive the Drone has the ability to produce and spread the nest jelly that forms the basis of the Hive. The nest jelly is an organic, wax like substance that breaks down nutrients from the soil, and creatures cocooned within it, and transfer it, through veins within the Jelly itself, to the genetic pools, and Hive structure-organs. The Drone's most important ability is it's ability to morph into the organ-structures of the Hive. One that will eventually store genetic memory, and produce larvae and the other horrors of the Swarm.<br /> <b>Description</b>: The Drone is an oversized, and matured larvae in many ways. It's body is a long, and sinuous with thick chitin. It has short legs keeping it's body low to the ground. It's tail ends with a nasty stinger that drips with a vile, green liquid. It's head is characterized by multiple eyes dotting it's 'face', and an insect like mandible that drips a thick, viscous material. IIt has two arms that end in fine, clawed manipulators allowing it to shape and structure the jelly. <br /> <br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 3, Strength 5,<br /> Dexterity 3, Stamina 4, Presence 1, Manipulation 1, Composure<br /> 3<br /> <b>Skills</b>: Athletics 4, Brawl 3, Stealth 3, Survival 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Danger Sense, Iron Stamina 3, Iron Stomach, Natural<br /> Immunity, Toxin Resistance, Strong Back<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 5<br /> <b>Potency</b>: 1<br /> <b>Virtue:</b> -<br /> <b>Vice:</b> -<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 8<br /> <b>Defense</b>: 7<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13 (species factor 5)<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>WEAPONS/ATTACKS</b>:<br /> <b>Type Damage Dice Pool Range</b><br /> Spit 1 (L) 9 60/90/120<br /> Bite 2 (L) 8 <br /> Tail Stinger 2 (L) 8<br /> <br /> <b>ARMOR:</b><br /> <b>Type Rating Defense Penalty</b><br /> Chitin Hide 2/2 0<br /> <br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 5<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 Hivemind</b>: The Drone was born into the Brood. The Broodmother has <br /> complete and total domination of it's mind, and knows and sees every-<br /> thing that the Drone does. The Drone is <br /> <b>\u2022 Regeneration: </b>The Drone regains one point of Bashing or Lethal <br /> damage per round. It will prioritize Lethal above Bashing.<br /> <b>\u2022 Hive Jelly:</b> The Drone produces a thick, jelly like substance from<br /> it's throat. It can shape and mold this substance with it's hand. After a <br /> few minutes the top layer will develop into a strong, and flexible chitin<br /> to protect the veins below. When its used to cocoon a living target the<br /> same veins will attach to the victim and begin to liquidate them.<br /> <b>\u2022 Poison:</b> The Drone produces a low level poison with a Toxicity of 2.<br /> It's delivered through it's bite, spit or sting. It does damage once every<br /> hour until 24 hours have passed or the target has died. It deals Bashing<br /> damage, but can be increased to Lethal by spending a Essence point.<br /> <b>\u2022 </b> <b>Metamorphosis:</b> One of the Drone's most important abilities; when<br /> the Drone is upon a bed of Hive-jelly, and enough nutrients the Drone <br /> can meta-morph into organ-structure of the Hive; Hatcheries, dens or<br /> other such buildings that produce a variety of monsters. Organ-structures,<br /> as their name implies, are living things that bleed and heal. It takes<br /> a week to complete the transformation for every 2 Size it gain turning <br /> into the structure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Brood Warrior</span></b><br /> <img src=\"http://roleplayinfo.yolasite.com/resources/xenomorph___variation_by_doodle_bugz-d2y3n56.jpg.opt428x428o0,0s428x428.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> The staple, and most basic warrior template of the Brood uses the DNA of various terrestrial predators from wolves, great cats, et al and improved upon by the Brood's engineering. It's a fearless and efficient killing machine, using stealth, ambush, strength and tactics to overpower foes. Usually the second of the Brood to be hatched by a nascent Hive, the Warriors are adept at killing, or subduing living biomass to bring back to the Hive to help it flourish. <br /> <br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Intelligence 3, Wits 4, Resolve 3, Strength 6,<br /> Dexterity 5, Stamina 5, Presence 3, Manipulation 1, Composure<br /> 4<br /> <b>Skills</b>: Athletics 4, Brawl 5, Stealth 3, Survival 2, Intimidation 2<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Danger Sense, Iron Stamina 3, Iron Stomach, Natural <br /> Immunity, Toxin Resistance, Fast Reflexes 2<br /> <b>Specialties</b>: Athletics: Climbing, Jumping, Brawl: Claws,<br /> Stealth: In the Hive<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Potency</b>: 3<br /> <b>Virtue:</b> -<br /> <b>Vice:</b> -<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 10<br /> <b>Defense</b>: 9<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 19 (species factor 8)<br /> <b>Size:</b> 6<br /> <b>WEAPONS/ATTACKS</b>:<br /> <b>Type Damage Dice Pool Special</b><br /> Claws 2 (L) 12 AP 2, +1 Intiative<br /> Bite* 3 (L) 11 AP 1<br /> Tail Stinger 2 (L) 11 AP 1<br /> *The Bite must be used in a grapple.<br /> <br /> <b>ARMOR:</b><br /> <b>Type Rating Defense Penalty</b><br /> Chitin Hide 2/2 0<br /> <br /> <b>Health:</b> 9<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 12/3<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 Hivemind</b>: The warrior was born into the Brood. The Broodmother has <br /> complete and total domination of it's mind, and knows and sees every-<br /> thing that the warrior does. A Brood can not be surprised in combat as <br /> unless every Brood in the area is similarly caught by surprise. <br /> <b>\u2022 Regeneration: </b>The warrior regains two point of Bashing or Lethal <br /> damage per round. It will prioritize Lethal above Bashing.<br /> <b>\u2022 Poison:</b> The warrior produces a low level poison with a Toxicity of 2.<br /> It's delivered through it's bite or sting. It does damage once every<br /> thirty minutes, this time can be lowered by a minute per Essence spent,<br /> until 24 hours have passed or the target has died. It deals Bashing<br /> damage, but can be increased to Lethal by spending a Essence point.<br /> <b>\u2022 </b> <b>For the Swarm!</b>:The Brood regains a point of Willpower every time it takes <br /> a beneficial action for the Swarm. It can only happen once per event (e.g. It will get <br /> a point of Willpower for intercepting and attacking a threat, but it won't get a new point<br /> every round it attacks.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Jo